 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and complete: each of signCount, signSum, tarskiQuery, lagrangeCoeff, fullMatrix and fullInverse carries its def-form restatement, cardinality characterization, edge cases and both inverse laws, with bodies unexposed via `(rfl)` and no compatibility artifacts. The sole `private` (signSum_prod) hides no content, since the public signSum_prod_pow specializes to it, and an `Invertible` instance for fullMatrix is not type-correct because the matrix is rectangular in its index types.",
